Below you find  

1) a quick mapping of the most important columns for the question,  
2) a reminder of the filter you will repeatedly use (December‑2020), and  
3) ten different SELECT‑only BigQuery statements – from very simple exploration queries to the final one that returns the channel with the 4‑th highest number of sessions.  
Every query is limited to 20 rows so you can run them safely in the public sample project.

-------------------------------------------------
1.  Relevant columns and their “potential usage”

• `event_date`            : filter the month (December 2020 → ‘20201201’ … ‘20201231’).  
• `event_name`            : pick only the session starting hits (`session_start`).  
• `event_params`          : repeated record that contains the `source`, `medium`, and `ga_session_id` keys that are needed for channel grouping and session counting.  
• `user_pseudo_id`        : pseudo‑user identifier; together with `ga_session_id` this gives a unique session.  
• `traffic_source.*`      : alternative place where Google automatically stores default source / medium values (useful for comparison).  
• `platform` / `geo.*` / `device.*` : optional – can be used for additional breakdowns of the December traffic once channel numbers are known.

-------------------------------------------------
2.  Useful constant conditions

```text
-- Time window
WHERE event_date BETWEEN '20201201' AND '20201231'

-- Pick session starts only
AND event_name = 'session_start'

-- Build one session id
CONCAT(user_pseudo_id,'-',CAST(ga_sess_id AS STRING))      -- ga_sess_id extracted from event_params
```

-------------------------------------------------
3.  Ten exploratory / analytical queries
(Replace nothing – the project, dataset and tables already exist.  They all use the suffix wildcard pattern `events_202012*` to cover every December table.)

```sql
--Description: 1) Quick look – all available December tables and their row counts
SELECT
  _TABLE_SUFFIX AS table_for_december,
  COUNT(1)      AS rows_in_table
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_202012*`
GROUP BY table_for_december
ORDER BY table_for_december
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 2) Show 20 raw rows of one December day
SELECT *
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_20201201`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 3) What event names exist in December?
SELECT DISTINCT event_name
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_202012*`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 4) How many session_start hits per day?
SELECT
  event_date,
  COUNTIF(event_name = 'session_start') AS sessions_starting
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_202012*`
GROUP BY event_date
ORDER BY event_date
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 5) Inspect source / medium parameters inside a single day
SELECT
  user_pseudo_id,
  ep_source.value.string_value  AS source,
  ep_medium.value.string_value  AS medium
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_20201205`,
UNNEST(event_params) ep_source WITH OFFSET
JOIN UNNEST(event_params) ep_medium WITH OFFSET
  ON ep_source.key  = 'source'
 AND ep_medium.key  = 'medium'
 AND ep_source.offset = ep_medium.offset
WHERE event_name = 'session_start'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 6) Distinct combinations of source / medium (December)
WITH params AS (
  SELECT
    user_pseudo_id,
    (SELECT value.string_value FROM UNNEST(event_params) WHERE key = 'medium') AS medium,
    (SELECT value.string_value FROM UNNEST(event_params) WHERE key = 'source') AS source
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_202012*`
  WHERE event_name = 'session_start'
)
SELECT DISTINCT source, medium
FROM params
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 7) Build one session id (user_pseudo_id + ga_session_id) and verify uniqueness
WITH sessions AS (
  SELECT
    CONCAT(user_pseudo_id,'-',CAST(
           (SELECT value.int_value FROM UNNEST(event_params) WHERE key='ga_session_id')
         AS STRING)) AS session_id
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_202012*`
  WHERE event_name = 'session_start'
)
SELECT
  session_id,
  COUNT(*) AS hits_in_session_start   -- should be 1 for proper data
FROM sessions
GROUP BY session_id
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 8) Apply the Google‑style channel grouping rules to every session
WITH dec_session AS (
  SELECT
    session_id,
    (SELECT value.string_value FROM UNNEST(event_params) WHERE key='source') AS src,
    (SELECT value.string_value FROM UNNEST(event_params) WHERE key='medium') AS med
  FROM (
    SELECT
      CONCAT(user_pseudo_id,'-',CAST(
             (SELECT value.int_value FROM UNNEST(event_params) WHERE key='ga_session_id')
           AS STRING)) AS session_id,
      event_params,
      event_name
    FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_202012*`
    WHERE event_name='session_start'
  )
),
channels AS (
  SELECT
    session_id,
    src,
    med,
    /* very simplified rule‑set – extend if you need all channels */
    CASE
      WHEN src = '(direct)' AND med IN ('(not set)','(none)')                    THEN 'Direct'
      WHEN LOWER(med) IN ('display','banner','expandable','interstitial','cpm')  THEN 'Display'
      WHEN LOWER(med) = 'referral'                                               THEN 'Referral'
      WHEN LOWER(med) LIKE '%email%' OR LOWER(src) LIKE '%email%'               THEN 'Email'
      ELSE 'Unassigned'
    END AS channel
  FROM dec_session
)
SELECT *
FROM channels
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 9) Total December sessions per channel (top 20)
WITH dec_session AS (
  SELECT
    session_id,
    (SELECT value.string_value FROM UNNEST(event_params) WHERE key='source') AS src,
    (SELECT value.string_value FROM UNNEST(event_params) WHERE key='medium') AS med
  FROM (
    SELECT
      CONCAT(user_pseudo_id,'-',CAST(
             (SELECT value.int_value FROM UNNEST(event_params) WHERE key='ga_session_id')
           AS STRING)) AS session_id,
      event_params,
      event_name
    FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_202012*`
    WHERE event_name='session_start'
  )
),
channels AS (
  SELECT
    session_id,
    CASE
      WHEN src = '(direct)' AND med IN ('(not set)','(none)')                    THEN 'Direct'
      WHEN LOWER(med) IN ('display','banner','expandable','interstitial','cpm')  THEN 'Display'
      WHEN LOWER(med) = 'referral'                                               THEN 'Referral'
      WHEN LOWER(med) LIKE '%email%' OR LOWER(src) LIKE '%email%'               THEN 'Email'
      ELSE 'Unassigned'
    END AS channel
  FROM dec_session
)
SELECT
  channel,
  COUNT(DISTINCT session_id) AS sessions
FROM channels
GROUP BY channel
ORDER BY sessions DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 10) Final answer – pick the channel ranked #4 by December sessions
WITH dec_session AS (
  SELECT
    session_id,
    (SELECT value.string_value FROM UNNEST(event_params) WHERE key='source') AS src,
    (SELECT value.string_value FROM UNNEST(event_params) WHERE key='medium') AS med
  FROM (
    SELECT
      CONCAT(user_pseudo_id,'-',CAST(
             (SELECT value.int_value FROM UNNEST(event_params) WHERE key='ga_session_id')
           AS STRING)) AS session_id,
      event_params,
      event_name
    FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_202012*`
    WHERE event_name='session_start'
  )
),
channels AS (
  SELECT
    session_id,
    CASE
      WHEN src = '(direct)' AND med IN ('(not set)','(none)')                    THEN 'Direct'
      WHEN LOWER(med) IN ('display','banner','expandable','interstitial','cpm')  THEN 'Display'
      WHEN LOWER(med) = 'referral'                                               THEN 'Referral'
      WHEN LOWER(med) LIKE '%email%' OR LOWER(src) LIKE '%email%'               THEN 'Email'
      ELSE 'Unassigned'
    END AS channel
  FROM dec_session
),
ranked AS (
  SELECT
    channel,
    COUNT(DISTINCT session_id) AS sessions,
    DENSE_RANK() OVER(ORDER BY COUNT(DISTINCT session_id) DESC) AS rnk
  FROM channels
  GROUP BY channel
)
SELECT channel, sessions
FROM ranked
WHERE rnk = 4
LIMIT 20;
```

